# slice-retro ignore (ywr-harness ADR 0017) — files exempt from the UNMAPPED check.
#
# One POSIX ERE per line, matched against the full repo-relative path (anchored at both ends).
# Blank lines and `#` comments are skipped.
#
# THIS FILE IS THE VISIBLE SPEC-DEBT REGISTER, and that is its more important job. A group marked
# "spec candidate" has ADR coverage but no living spec yet — writing the spec deletes the group.
# A permanently exempt group (generated code, plumbing with no behavior of its own) says so.
#
# Keep the comments. An ignore list without reasons becomes a list nobody dares delete from.
#
# SEED: placed once by /ywr-harness:harness-init and never overwritten. It is yours to edit.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Examples — delete these and write your own. They are shaped from a real register so the
# intended granularity is visible: exempt a named file or a tight group, never a whole subtree.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# generated — no human writes these, so no spec can describe them
# src/lib/api-types\.ts

# app wiring / plumbing — no spec-worthy behavior of its own
# src/.*/__init__\.py
# src/main\.py
# src/config\.py

# spec candidate: admin console (ADR 00NN) — has a decision record, no living spec yet.
# Delete this group when the spec lands.
# src/admin/.*\.py
